  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Old Ghost Bai Jun refuses to kill Fang Leng and Fang Yun outright because Fang clan is a Western Desert super force. He names Fang Di Chang as Fang clan’s second supreme elder and a famous wisdom path expert of Western Desert, and worries that if Fang clan searches green ghost desert it will hinder his master’s plan.",
      "chapters": [
        1504
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_old_ghost_bai_jun",
        "char_fang_leng",
        "char_fang_yun",
        "fac_fang_clan",
        "reg_western_desert"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a plain face and ordinary appearance.",
      "chapters": [
        1520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan, planning how to approach that nearest super force, treats Fang clan’s first supreme elder as rank eight and Fang Di Chang as a wisdom path great expert renowned in Fang Yuan’s first life, with wisdom path great grandmaster attainment, and marked in Shadow Sect’s information.",
      "chapters": [
        1505
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wisdom-path-attainment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_shadow_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan expects the second supreme elder, a wisdom path great grandmaster with rank seven cultivation, to come as strategist. Inquiry Dock appears in the sky. Fang Di Chang tells Fang Hua Sheng they have a tracking method on Divine Bean Palace, need to repair Fallen Flower Hall, and will combine three houses to create the battlefield killer move peach blossom maze. He then leaves Inquiry Dock to meet Fang Yuan in Fallen Flower Hall, the first time they meet. His immortal aura is utterly concealed. Fang Yuan cannot sense anything from the plain, ordinary face, and takes that as worthy of a wisdom path great grandmaster.",
      "chapters": [
        1520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "strategy-meeting",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_inquiry_dock",
        "char_fang_hua_sheng",
        "house_divine_bean_palace",
        "house_fallen_flower_hall"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As wisdom path great grandmaster and second supreme elder he leads Fang clan’s expedition. Fang Yuan, still inside Inquiry Dock, praises peach blossom maze for exposing Divine Bean Palace, which should have been hidden deep under the desert. Fang Di Chang names Divine Bean Palace’s immortal killer move green armor vegetable garden, and says Fang clan knows only the name and appearance.",
      "chapters": [
        1522
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "divine-bean-palace-exposed",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside Inquiry Dock he frowns that even Fang Zhi’s poisonous cloud arrow sparrow is useless, then orders the immortals back so peach blossom maze can attack. The maze can trap rank eight Gu Immortals. It grows a forest, sends jade light waves, then blooming peach blossoms that form flowery wind warriors. He asks Suan Bu Jin to control part of them, and is shocked when that enslavement path method takes an immemorial soul beast. He promises heavy compensation, then is furious at being extorted because Fang clan lacks a strong enslavement path expert.",
      "chapters": [
        1523
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "maze-attack",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zhi",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He recognizes Chen Yi as Heavenly Lotus Sect’s first supreme elder. As a wisdom path great grandmaster he argues that Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable left Divine Bean Palace in Western Desert, so it belongs to Western Desert. Fang Yuan treats the two rounds of rank seven attacks as Fang Di Chang’s plan, a cover for Fang Gong. Even as a wisdom path great grandmaster, Fang Di Chang was only rank seven. Green ghost desert dao marks corrode peach blossom maze, soul beasts rush in, and he cannot solve it while the first supreme elder is still fighting inside. Fang Yuan tells him he can help Fang clan obtain the Immortal Gu House.",
      "chapters": [
        1527
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "palace-stalemate",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chen_yi",
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect",
        "char_genesis_lotus_immortal_venerable",
        "char_fang_gong",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan comes to Fang clan headquarters and changes appearance to Fang Di Chang. He tells them he is Suan Bu Jin, who also became Fang Di Chang. Fang clan realizes their second supreme elder was replaced. Fang Gong treats him as the murderer of that second supreme elder. Fang Yuan says that saying Fang Di Chang died at his hands is both correct and wrong: the body is destroyed, but the soul is in Fang Yuan’s hands. To avoid soul lantern Gu, Fang Yuan had separated body and soul rather than kill him, and still keeps that soul.",
      "chapters": [
        2101
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "headquarters-talk",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_soul_lantern_gu"
      ]
    }
  ],
